c.feedback_and_homing:
The SCS0009 reports absolute position (10 bit over 300 deg), load, temperature and voltage over the bus, so the arm angle is servo angle / 1.5 + offset.

The clutch can slip on a hand push, and then the offset changes. Homing (at power-up, and whenever the load register shows an unexpected peak during free motion):
- set the torque limit to 15 % (0.043 N·m at the arm, below the 0.06 clutch, so the clutch does not slip during homing);
- drive slowly to a hard stop at −50 deg: a lug in the arm hub hits a pin on the end of the static ring, hidden inside the arm;
- detect the stall from load/position and store the new offset (~1 s).

Optional instead of the stop: a magnet in the arm hub + a hall sensor in the static plug (wires stay static).

